# Line endings: text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF, whatever the editor or tool wrote.
# Git converts on `git add`, so an editor writing CRLF cannot flip a whole file in a commit (a one-line change
# showing as a whole-file diff hides real changes in review). Rules: research/docs/conventions.md, "Line endings".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files: CRLF in the working tree (cmd.exe misreads labels in LF batch files).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Byte for byte, never converted: raw measurement captures (vendored code shipped as its authors ship it goes here too).
research/docs/data/** -text

# Binary.
